00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.000
The week's biggest developments pulled together, what actually moved, why it matters,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:41.720
and what to watch next. This week, the NASDAQ composite closed at 25,889,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:48.500
after swinging through a 2% drop midweek and a 2.5% rebound on the Iran deal news.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:57.440
The S&amp;P 500 ended at 7,431, while the TSX composite reached 34,938.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:04.140
Partfolio cumulative return, year-to-date return, and alpha versus the NASDAQ are not available

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:10.160
in today's data, so I will not report them. The dominant thread was geopolitical relief

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:15.500
from reported progress on a Iran deal that cut oil prices more than 4%

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.600
and lifted financials on expected trading revenue.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:27.960
Sticky inflation readings at 4.2% CPI and 6.5% PPI kept both the bank of Canada and the Fed

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:34.620
on hold with limited easing priced in. Index inclusion effects, long cycle infrastructure spending,

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:39.760
and first mover modes in healthcare also shaped positioning across the five trading sessions.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.160
Index inclusion creates a mechanical buying wave that can produce

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.160
outsized short-term moves even when fundamentals have not changed.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:55.640
Marvell Technologies addition to the S&amp;P 500 at the end of June triggered a 7% plus pre-market jump,

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:00.300
illustrating how passive funds must rebalance regardless of valuation.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:06.420
The strategy works best when the added stock already has sector momentum and above average

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:11.800
trading volume. It carries the risk that the move reverses once the rebalancing is complete.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:17.440
To implement screen for stocks with upcoming index announcements using your broker's news feed

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:23.940
or ETF holdings reports, then size the position smaller than a pure fundamental trade because

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.980
the catalyst has a known expiration. Historical data shows these inclusion pops have delivered the

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:35.600
strongest alpha in the first three trading sessions after announcement. Risk management requires

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.340
a tight stop just below the pre-announcement close once the initial surge fades.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:46.460
Air Canada and the International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers reached a

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.720
tentative agreement on a new contract this week according to BNN Bloomberg.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:57.680
The deal covers approximately 9,000 workers across the carrier's operations and addresses wages,

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:03.140
scheduling, and pension contributions that had been in dispute since the prior round of bargaining.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:08.880
Both sides confirmed the agreement ends the immediate threat of job action that had been scheduled

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:14.640
for later this month. Union leadership stated the package includes improvements to job security

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:20.380
language and training provisions that were not in the previous contract. Air Canada indicated

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.680
the tentative terms will now move to a ratification vote expected within the next several weeks.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:31.560
The resolution removes one near-term labor overhang that had weighed on the stock during the first

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:38.440
half of June. Retailers including IKEA are accelerating expansion of small format stores as a response

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:44.720
to shifting consumer patterns and rising real estate expenses. The Swedish furniture giant opened

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:51.160
or announced more than 40 compact urban locations in the past 18 months across North America and

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:58.040
Europe each averaging roughly one-third the size of a traditional big box outlet. Company executives

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:04.700
cited faster inventory terms and lower operating costs per square foot as the primary drivers behind

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:11.200
the shift. BNN Bloomberg reported that similar moves are underway at other chains seeking to

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:16.840
maintain physical presence in high-density neighborhoods without the capital outlay of full-size stores.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:23.160
Early results show these locations achieve higher sales per square foot while requiring fewer staff

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:29.080
hours to operate. The trend coincides with post-pandemic changes in shopping behavior that favor

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:34.580
quick in-and-out visits over large format browsing. Earnings reports scheduled for the coming

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:40.360
week include canopy growth and Kruger, both of which will provide fresh data on consumer staples

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:46.080
margins under the latest producer price pressures. Canopy growth is expected to release quarterly

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:51.560
results that will show whether recent cost-cutting measures have offset continued softness in recreational

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:58.220
cannabis demand. Kruger will report on grocery pricing power and same store sales trends after

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:05.740
the 6.5% PPI print highlighted elevated input costs across the sector. Analysts will watch both

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:11.160
companies for any commentary on how higher energy and packaging expenses are being passed through

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:17.640
to customers without triggering volume declines. The releases arrive ahead of the Bank of Canada's

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:24.300
July 15th decision and could influence sentiment toward defensive equity sleeves. Investors using

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:30.620
TFSA accounts can monitor these names for potential margin expansion signals that align with the

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:36.720
inflation protected strategy discussed earlier. Another city has deployed additional transit police

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:43.140
to address safety concerns and fair evasion according to BNN Bloomberg reporting. The initiative

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:48.720
follows similar programs in other major North American municipalities that have reported measurable

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:53.720
reductions in incidents after increasing officer presence on platforms and trains.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:06:00.800
City officials cited a 23% rise in fair evasion complaints over the past year as the immediate trigger

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:06.640
for the expanded deployment. The program includes both uniform patrols and plain clothes and

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:12.680
enforcement teams focused on high traffic corridors. Local transit authorities indicated the added

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.920
staffing is funded through a combination of municipal budget reallocations and provincial grants.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:23.960
The move reflects broader municipal efforts to restore writer confidence after pandemic error

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:30.660
ridership declines. Meta continues internal efforts to commercialize the new AI model developed

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:37.880
after hiring Alexander Wang a year ago according to CNBC. Wang, previously founder of Scale AI,

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:44.200
was brought in to accelerate Meta's large language model capabilities. Yet the company has struggled to

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.560
integrate the resulting technology into its core advertising and consumer products.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:54.100
Mark Zuckerberg has taken direct responsibility for driving adoption across business units,

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:58.840
a shift that underscores the gap between model development and monetization.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:05.380
Internal documents obtained by CNBC show that early versions of the model achieve competitive bench

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:10.440
mark scores but lacked clear use cases that justified additional infrastructure spend.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:16.240
The episode illustrates the execution risk that remains even after high profile talent

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:22.660
acquisitions in the AI space. Canadian investors tracking global tech exposure may note the story

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:28.320
as a reminder that hiring announcements along do not guarantee near-term revenue contribution.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:35.320
President Trump is traveling to the G7 summit in France with the Iran deal and Ukraine on the formal

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:42.000
agenda CNBC reported. The meetings occur against the backdrop of reported progress toward ending the

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:48.620
Iran conflict that already produced a 4% drop in oil prices this week. European leaders are expected

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:54.760
to press for coordinated energy security measures should the deal hold while the Ukraine file remains

00:07:54.760 --> 00:08:00.840
a separate track with limited linkage to the current ceasefire talks. White House officials indicated

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:06.340
the summit will also address tariff and trade issues that have resurfaced after the recent inflation

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:12.100
prints. Markets will watch for any language that signals follow through commitments versus rhetorical

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:18.240
progress. The outcome could influence whether the current oil price relief proves durable into July.

